60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Based on the evidence, a Meeting Space is the most reasonable choice. It eliminates the external rental costs and provides a necessary venue for private discussions without the maintenance risks associated with a kitchen.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I concur. A Meeting Space offers the sanctuary we need for honest, private communication, ensuring that difficult conversations no longer happen in front of everyone. It is the most compassionate choice for our collective well-being.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,I still think we're ignoring the daily grind. A Meeting Space doesn't stop the crumbs or the twenty-five-minute walks. An Open Kitchen actually improves our quality of life every single day. I vote for Option A.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"May, your ""quality of life"" argument is just a preference for shorter walks. The data shows a clear financial drain and a lack of privacy. Option C is the only rational choice. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"We have seen that our current state is one of noise and clutter. While a kitchen serves the body, a Meeting Space provides the dignity of privacy and the wisdom of order. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, your point about the daily grind is noted, but the risk of unfair maintenance is too high. A Meeting Space is a structured solution that benefits everyone equally. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"It is clear that we all value a better environment, but the need for a space that protects our dignity during difficult moments is paramount. I believe Option C is the most thoughtful path. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"You're all just ignoring the actual time we lose! A meeting room is just another place to sit and talk, but a kitchen gives us our time back. I'm sticking with Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your passion for lunch is admirable, but we're discussing a business asset, not a cafeteria. The financial leak and the privacy void are the real problems here. I'm staying with Option C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"It is often the case that the loudest need is not the most profound one. While hunger is a physical reality, the need for harmony and respect in our communication is a spiritual necessity. I remain with Option C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I have already cast my vote for Option C. The evidence regarding external costs and the need for privacy outweighs the convenience of a kitchen. I see no reason to change my position.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I have also cast my vote for Option C. It is the only choice that addresses the emotional distance between us and provides a safe harbor for the conversations we cannot have at our desks.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,You're all acting like a few minutes of walking is a tragedy compared to a little bit of cleaning! I'm the only one thinking about our actual daily energy. I'm staying with Option A.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, it's not a tragedy, it's just inefficient. But paying for outside rooms for four people is a genuine waste. I've made my choice; the logic is undeniable. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"The path we have chosen is one of balance and respect. By prioritizing a space for meaningful dialogue, we heal the fractures in our community. I cast my final vote for Option C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"The consensus is clear. While the convenience of a kitchen is appealing, the data on financial waste and the need for privacy make the Meeting Space the only logical and sustainable choice. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe we have found the most gentle and effective solution. By choosing the Meeting Space, we provide ourselves with the grace of privacy and the opportunity to truly know one another. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"Fine, you've all won. I'll keep walking for my lunch and cleaning up my own crumbs, but don't come complaining to me when you're all starving during your ""meaningful dialogues."" I vote for Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"It's a pity you can't see the logic, May, but the numbers don't lie. We've stopped the financial leak and solved the privacy issue. A victory for rationality. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a blessing that we have reached an agreement. Though we differ in our desires, we have found a common purpose in seeking dignity and order. I cast my final vote for Option C.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
